-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/0cc7d47c-d469-4065-bdbf-7e4d289a7429
-- title:
--   Gathering exactly the masks of positive reporting children
-- statement:
--   Fix a finite raw incidence set $I$, wanted label $w$, prefix $u$, and depth $k<J$. Enumerate the $G=\binom{2h}{h}$ balanced children in their defined order, and let $s_0,\ldots,s_{t-1}$ be precisely the child indices whose depth-$k+1$ prefix counts are positive. Memory stores these indices and the left and right masks $L_i,R_i$ of all children.
--
--   All five arrays must fit within space $S$. The index array is disjoint from both destinations; the left source is disjoint from the left destination; the right source is disjoint from both destinations; and the destinations are disjoint. Assume $S\le B$, $2^{J(512h)+1}\le B$, and $d<D$. The fixed pair-gather program terminates within $80t+80$ steps and writes
--   $$\nu(\mathrm{dst}_L+j)=L_{s_j},\qquad\nu(\mathrm{dst}_R+j)=R_{s_j}\quad(j<t).$$
--   These are exactly the positive children's masks in their retained order; all other cells are preserved.
--
--   This connects physical mask gathering to the abstract reporting frontier.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/c0ldzy17/three-sum-lean/blob/2b639655e07421b9ac743de9090459bab473a7c0/Submission/ThreeSum/LightReportingPositiveMasks.lean#L37-L102

